.SH SMART INSTALL AND PACKAGE SUFFIXES
Source packages use the filename suffix
.B .src.bcraft
and installable packages use
.BR .bcraft .
Both formats remain gzip-compressed tar archives internally.
The suffix identifies the file as a bcraft package; bcraft still validates the
package contents and metadata instead of trusting the filename alone.
.PP
When
.B install
is given a package whose name is already installed, bcraft compares version
and release.  If the supplied package is newer, bcraft asks whether the
installed package should be updated.  A positive answer enters the same update
code path as an explicit
.B update
command.  The default answer is no.  If the versions are identical, install
reports that the package is already installed.  If the supplied package is
older, install refuses the downgrade.  The explicit
.B update
command remains available for scripts and for users who intentionally request
an update operation.
